{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q21098997","formula":"C₁₁H₁₄ClNO₂","hill":"C11H14ClNO2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":14.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"6-chloro-MDMA"},"descriptions":{"en":"6-Chloro-MDMA, also known as 6-chloro-3,4-methylenedioxy-N-methylamphetamine or as 2-chloro-4,5-methylenedioxy-N-methylamphetamine (2-Cl-4,5-MDMA), is a chemical compound of the phenethylamine, amphetamine, and MDxx families related to MDMA. It is the 6-chloro derivative of MDMA. The drug has been identified both in seized \"ecstasy\" tablets and in urine samples from drug users. It is thought most likely to be an impurity from synthesis and its pharmacological properties have not been established; however, it has been banned in several countries."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":60209987,"mass":227.69,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(CC1=CC2=C(C=C1Cl)OCO2)NC","inchikey":"UUGIOXDVHPQROZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(6-chloro-1,3-benzodioxol-5-yl)-N-methylpropan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"60209987","atoms":29,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.23,"y":-1.067,"z":-0.642,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.783,"y":-0.455,"z":0.689,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.874,"y":0.785,"z":0.502,"el":"C"},{"x":0.484,"y":0.464,"z":-0.094,"el":"C"},{"x":1.452,"y":-0.127,"z":0.744,"el":"C"},{"x":2.688,"y":-0.432,"z":0.214,"el":"C"},{"x":2.994,"y":-0.175,"z":-1.099,"el":"C"},{"x":2.083,"y":0.401,"z":-1.955,"el":"C"},{"x":0.818,"y":0.722,"z":-1.447,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.307,"y":1.441,"z":-2.546,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.26,"y":-0.551,"z":-1.419,"el":"O"},{"x":4.717,"y":-1.076,"z":-0.155,"el":"C"},{"x":3.722,"y":-1.001,"z":0.888,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.933,"y":-0.191,"z":1.576,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.892,"y":0.783,"z":1.074,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.725,"y":-0.334,"z":-1.287,"el":"H"},{"x":